Patch-Id: ASTRA-0004
Title: New crate toolkit/components/astra_blocker_engine (Brave adblock-rust engine, C++ hook bridge, Rust/XPCOM management service)
Tier: P2
Upstream-Files: toolkit/components/moz.build, toolkit/components/astra_blocker_engine/Cargo.toml, toolkit/components/astra_blocker_engine/moz.build, toolkit/components/astra_blocker_engine/cbindgen.toml, toolkit/components/astra_blocker_engine/components.conf, toolkit/components/astra_blocker_engine/nsIAstraBlockerService.idl, toolkit/components/astra_blocker_engine/src/lib.rs, toolkit/components/astra_blocker_engine/AstraBlocker.h, toolkit/components/astra_blocker_engine/AstraBlocker.cpp, toolkit/components/astra_blocker_engine/AstraBlockerService.h, toolkit/components/astra_blocker_engine/AstraBlockerService.cpp
Intent: add the Astra blocker engine crate (new files, no upstream code touched except the one DIRS registration line); mirrors toolkit/components/content-classifier/content_classifier_engine for the adblock 0.12.1 dependency and cbindgen FFI, but serves first- and third-party Astra verdicts, stores scriptlet/redirect resources, exposes cosmetic selectors and bounded stats through nsIAstraBlockerService, and installs rules from the Host API Blocker module. Engine logic and list/resource parsing live in Rust; the C++ files are the channel hook and the XPCOM glue the pinned Gecko ABI requires.
Risk: medium (new code, but self-contained in one directory + one DIRS line; adblock 0.12.1 already vendored and audited, so `mach vendor rust` is a no-op; the XPCOM service is a singleton registered by components.conf)
Test: tools/blocker-wiring-check.sh; `mach build -j2`; live probe `tools/marionette-probe/blocker-probe.py`; see docs/astra/BLOCKER.md
Verified-On: 153.6.0
Removal-Plan: delete the directory + the DIRS line if the blocker moves out of tree (fallback proxy); new-file entries need the forge lint new-file carve-out (see BLOCKER_WIRING.md section 6)
---
